think Read the crypto README, design wave, and the two itineraries. The staged-but-unsent kumara_path lap was complete and its witness GREEN — so the first move was to send it as its own signed round to origin and xykj61 (send often).
think For the next crux: the identity arc reached its account-path leaf (kumara_path) but had NO composition tying the whole arc together. kumara/README.md shows a Kumara identity begins with an ed25519 keypair from a 32-byte seed. The highest-Lindy front door is the one composition phrase → seed → path → keypair → signature — the identity-arc sibling of eth_address/bitcoin_address, what Kumara, Vault, Comlink, and the Lotus signed carry all reach identity through. Fully agent-doable over TEST seeds; the real key stays the custody gate.
think Studied signed_carry.rye for composition house style and confirmed the compose surface: bip39_seed.seed(out,mnemonic,passphrase); kumara_path.derive_identity(seed,coin,account,index)->Node; slip10.public_key(node)->33-byte 0x00-prefixed; ed25519_sign.derive_public/sign; ed25519_verify.verify. slip10.public_key IS ed25519.derive_public prefixed with 0x00, so the identity's raw 32-byte public key = slip10 form minus tag = ed25519_sign.derive_public — a strong internal consistency invariant to assert.
think Wrote crypto/kumara_identity.rye: from_seed and from_mnemonic (sharing identity_from_node so the two entry points cannot drift), plus sign/verify thin wrappers. One mechanical red — from_seed's error union named bip39.HmacError, which does not exist; imported hmac_sha512 and used hmac.HmacError. Then GREEN on metal.
think Proof three replayable ways, no fabricated constant: (1) the bip39 half anchored to BIP-39's OWN published Trezor vector seed byte-for-byte; (2) the arc proven drift-free (from_mnemonic = hand-wiring bip39_seed→kumara_path.derive_identity, from_seed reaches the identical identity, three-way public-key agreement, the ed25519 half proven one rung down against SLIP-0010's own vectors); (3) the derived key a real working signing key by a sign→verify round-trip with three refusals (flipped message, flipped signature, wrong key). Determinism, distinctness, and the hardened-offset edge close it.
obs Registered the new witness in the suite; the count guard went from 51 to 52 files GREEN (35 primitives + 17 compositions). Synced crypto/README.md, docs/CRYPTO.md, and the suite's spelled counts 51→52; tame_style_check bans clean.
obs Non-gated: TEST identities only from published vectors, no network, no funds, no device. Growing a REAL Kumara identity from the maintainer's own phrase and signing a real record with it stays the custody gate (#3/#4) — this library derives and verifies a test identity; it never holds the key.
